    <innerclass refid="classClinicAppointment" prot="public">ClinicAppointment</innerclass>
    <briefdescription>
<para><ref refid="classAppointment" kindref="compound">Appointment</ref> entity defined in this header, bound to the clinics appointment table. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>This is a minimal concrete specialisation of <ref refid="classAppointment" kindref="compound">Appointment</ref>. It fixes only the table name (&quot;clinics_appointments&quot;) and provides a constructor, a table-name accessor and a destructor. It does not define an organisation name or the static permission-query helpers that the other appointment specialisations expose.</para>
<para>WHY THIS FILE MATTERS IN THE SERVER: It gives callers a ready-made <ref refid="classAppointment" kindref="compound">Appointment</ref> for the clinics appointment table when only the table name is needed. Note that the class is named <ref refid="classClinicAppointment" kindref="compound">ClinicAppointment</ref>, the same name used in <ref refid="clinic_8hpp" kindref="compound">entities/appointments/clinic.hpp</ref>, so including both headers together would conflict. It is kept as a lightweight alternative for code paths that do not need permission helpers.</para>
<para>CONCEPTS TO LEARN (for beginners):<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>std::optional: <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Static constexpr member: a compile-time constant stored on the class, usable without an object.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>One Definition Rule: two different classes with the same name in the same namespace will clash if both headers are included in one translation unit; that is the caveat noted for this file.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para><simplesect kind="author"><para>Amr Osman <ulink url="mailto:dr3mro@gmail.com">dr3mro@gmail.com</ulink> </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="date"><para>2026-11-16 </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
